{"name":"Lauren’s Surprise","hex":"#d5e5e7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"surprise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something unexpected.","A mess of feces, left by a pet or small child in an unexpected place or at an unexpected time."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (someone) to feel unusually alarmed or delighted by something unexpected.","To do something to (a person) that they are not expecting, as a surprise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surprise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Surprise","blocks":[{"text":"Surprise is a rapid, fleeting mental and physiological state. It is related to the startle response experienced by animals and humans as the result of an unexpected event."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Charles_Bell%2C_Essays_on_the_anatomy_of_Wellcome_L0031951.jpg/330px-Charles_Bell%2C_Essays_on_the_anatomy_of_Wellcome_L0031951.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surprise","wikidata":"Q333173"},{"title":"Lauren","blocks":[{"text":"Lauren is mostly a feminine given name. The name's meaning may be \"laurel tree\", \"sweet of honor\", or \"wisdom\". It is derived from the French name Laurence, a feminine version of Laurent, which is in turn derived from the Roman surname Laurentius."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lauren","wikidata":"Q2274625"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg/500px-STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg/1280px-STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg/500px-STS-51L_riadiace_stred